From 984851b24528608c78898592cdc3908f92d73904 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 09:12:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] soc/integration: drop SoCCore.add_csr /
 add_memory_region / add_csr_region
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

These three methods on SoCCore were thin wrappers over the canonical
APIs that have been the documented way to do these things since the
SoCBusHandler / SoCCSRHandler refactor:

    soc.add_csr(name, ...)            -> soc.csr.add(name, ...)
    soc.add_memory_region(name,
        origin, length, type=...)     -> soc.bus.add_region(name,
                                            SoCRegion(origin=origin,
                                                size=length,
                                                cached=...,
                                                linker=...))
    soc.add_csr_region(name,
        origin, busword, obj)         -> soc.csr_regions[name] = (
                                            SoCCSRRegion(origin,
                                                busword, obj))

Audit: zero in-tree callers (every `self.add_csr()` hit was on a
peripheral class — DMA, ICAP, HyperBus, PWM, SPIMaster, stream
Multiplexer / Demultiplexer — that defines its own add_csr method,
unrelated to SoCCore).

Out-of-tree code that still uses these will get a clean
AttributeError pointing at the call site; the migration is the
1-line substitution shown above.

Verified: SoCCore no longer exposes the three names;
test/test_wishbone.py passes 23/23; litex_boards digilent_arty
builds end-to-end with byte-identical 778 KB gateware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 litex/soc/integration/soc_core.py | 14 --------------
 1 file changed, 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/litex/soc/integration/soc_core.py b/litex/soc/integration/soc_core.py
index 25d80d156..35068ca00 100644
--- a/litex/soc/integration/soc_core.py
+++ b/litex/soc/integration/soc_core.py
@@ -285,20 +285,6 @@ class SoCCore(LiteXSoC):
     def csr_data_width(self):
         return self.csr.data_width
 
-    # Methods --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-
-    def add_csr(self, csr_name, csr_id=None, use_loc_if_exists=False):
-        self.csr.add(csr_name, csr_id, use_loc_if_exists=use_loc_if_exists)
-
-    def add_memory_region(self, name, origin, length, type="cached"):
-        self.bus.add_region(name, SoCRegion(origin=origin, size=length,
-            cached = "cached" in type,
-            linker = "linker" in type)
-        )
-
-    def add_csr_region(self, name, origin, busword, obj):
-        self.csr_regions[name] = SoCCSRRegion(origin, busword, obj)
-
 # SoCCore arguments --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
 def soc_core_args(parser):
